  "body": "Adds an inactive account-only social preview with chronological Following as the default, separate explainable Discover, explicit connection consent, follow/mute/block/dismiss controls and independent discovery/personalization preferences. Authenticated Servant handlers derive the actor from the token and call the PostgreSQL authority through parameterized queries. Legacy vCard QR generation now stays local, and social caches are account-scoped.\n\nDependencies: #366 and the preceding stack; generated mobile contract PR diegueins680/TDF-mobile#80. Keep draft and unmerged. SOCIAL_V2_ENABLED, social_v2_runtime.enabled and VITE_SOCIAL_V2_ENABLED remain false. No production migration or activation was performed.\n\nActual local evidence on the refreshed application source:\n- Four formal models passed; twelve unsafe configurations failed their specifically expected invariants/action properties. Relationships 101,855 states; Feed 1,674; RequestReplay 272; Reaction 15.\n- Thirty model-derived SQL transitions passed, including the repaired peer-consent ownership case, plus persistence/race/retry/revocation fixtures.\n- Eight real localhost HTTP examples passed with Servant bearer authentication and private PostgreSQL 16.10. Covers gates, injected actor, consent withdrawal, blocks, cursor/limit validation, membership revocation, inactive tokens and organizations.\n- Fifteen focused web tests passed. Full web TypeScript/Vite build and bundle budget passed after canonical regeneration and upstream dependency refresh (357,190 gzip initial JS / five preloads).\n- Local synthetic component browser journey passed keyboard tabs, default Following, acceptance, 390px layout and selected axe rules. Screenshots were captured and inspected; this is not full-app or mobile E2E.\n- OpenAPI generators ran for the additive fragment and combined web/mobile contracts. Twelve workflow guard tests passed. CI uses fresh temporary browser artifacts to avoid uploading historical screenshots after an early failure.\n\nThe refreshed Stack-linked backend test binary passed 2,542 examples with zero failures. The separate application executable build and broader backend CI are tracked independently; historical 2,540-example results remain labeled historical. Current CI must be read at the current head. The HTTP interpreter failed on a GHC bytecode limit; object compilation passed. Docker API 500 blocked a later run; a private native PostgreSQL fallback passed without restarting shared Docker.\n\nIncomplete requirements: legacy DM/notification/search/fan-club/media block enforcement, token/delegated-entity identity, full lifecycle and worker refinement, mobile UI, long relationship pagination, private requests, general harassment reporting, old/new application coexistence, representative data and useful-outcome instrumentation. The disabled preview does not repair those production boundaries. See docs/social/handoff.md for each acceptance status and next implementation steps.\n\nRollback: pause the database and client/process behavior while preserving every new consent/block/tombstone/publication write. Do not route activated users to old endpoints that ignore blocks. Reconciliation is read-only and exercised on private fixtures; no destructive down migration.\n\nDeployment exception: a repository integration reported Vercel SUCCESS on audit #355; no deployment command was issued here. Exact-target inspection returned HTTP 403, so owner inspection/removal remains blocked. See docs/social/operations.md for the provider URL. Branch-scoped suppression and Cloudflare-specific skip prefixes are present, while correctness CI remains enabled. This prevents claiming that every deployment remained pending.\n\nFollow-up #377 now verifies the full schema-only fixture plus 102 registered migrations, additive reapplication, publication backfill and preserved-write pause. It passed native PostgreSQL 16.10 and the actual PostgreSQL 17 CI job at b689f88e2. This does not establish legacy application block enforcement or production lock duration.\n\n\n## Parent reconciliation \u2014 2026-09-16\n\nNormal merge `0bac512baed505f7f035f44c022fc0b64405b9e7` retains original head `9a68db7448909741b6084bfa41bfcfc55fba2597` and parent `6a6d9e02c22eee213cf56787d9de9e4252721fed` without rewriting either history. Six conflict resolutions preserve the existing social workflow, database tests and more complete client documentation. Current parent artwork/Instagram fixes remain intact. All five added reviewed catalog entries are preserved; only the obsolete switch-command decision for the replaced Instagram CLI is retired. Strict regenerated JSON and CSV pass with 1,114 reviewed candidates against mobile `c1832c5eb150299c12b36ba156ff38c981a6b046`.\n\nVerified locally: disposable PostgreSQL social migration/consent/retry/race/pause checks; four positive formal models and twelve required negative controls; repository quality; unchanged audit-ci policy; exact generated web/mobile/additive contracts; web lint and TypeScript. The full local web suite is still running and its outcome is not yet claimed. New hosted checks and any renewed review remain required. Existing social runtime, SQL, models, test scripts and social workflow are byte-identical to the original PR head. Preview/activation gates are unchanged; no manual deployment. This PR remains draft pending its documented readiness and stack requirements.\n\n\n### Reconciliation verification completed\n\nHosted CI is successful on exact `0bac512baed505f7f035f44c022fc0b64405b9e7`: 210 web suites / 1,994 tests plus lint, typecheck and production build; 2,542 backend examples; 67 mobile suites / 327 tests; 46 persona browser journeys; social client 3 suites / 15 tests plus browser/accessibility journey; and social models/PostgreSQL refinement checks. [Full CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35053708402), [social verification](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35053708473). General migration-tests was skipped by the unchanged path classifier; the dedicated social SQL checks actually ran.\n\nThe overloaded local full-web attempt reported timeouts/debounce failures in unchanged tests and was stopped with SIGTERM (exit 143) after the complete same-head hosted suite and build passed. That local attempt is not counted as passed, and its cause remains unproven; no assertion or timeout was altered. Local SQL, four positive/twelve negative formal checks, repository quality, exact web/mobile contracts, strict catalog JSON/CSV and the unchanged dependency-audit gate passed independently.\n\nThis resolves the parent-conflict/catalog repair. Native-stack integration and the documented inactive-preview/readiness boundaries remain; no partial stack merge, history rewrite or production activation was performed.\n",
